tools/.venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
*.egg-info/
packages/estimating-tools/build/
packages/bimforge/build/

# worktrees for parallel branch work (superpowers)
.worktrees/

# Caltrans standard-plan source files (DGN) and their DXF conversions -- large
# (79 MB) and re-downloadable from dot.ca.gov via manifest.json's per-sheet
# url + sha256, so they stay out of the repo.
#
# Note the trailing `*`: git will NOT re-include a path whose parent directory
# is itself excluded, so `/data/caltrans-2025/` (no star) would make the
# negations below silently do nothing.
/data/caltrans-2025/*
# ...but the hand-transcribed TABLES are ours, not a re-download: ~64 KB of
# diffable YAML that is the ground truth five gated tests check against
# (D80/D81 concrete CF/LF + LB/LF, B3 walls, D89 headwalls, D84 wingwalls).
# While they were excluded CI SKIPPED all five, so the strongest checks in the
# suite ran nowhere but one developer's disk.
!/data/caltrans-2025/tables/
# ...and the manifest is what makes ignoring the binaries safe in the first
# place: 27 KB recording which 91 sheets, from which URLs, at which sha256.
# Ignored alongside the very files it describes, it was self-defeating -- the
# only copy sat on the same disk as the 79 MB it was insurance for.
!/data/caltrans-2025/manifest.json

# brainstorming visual companion
.superpowers/
